  "created": "2022-05-02T01:52:30.967Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Say I have an overlapping contact receiver searching for the tag \"Damage\" and a sender sending \"Damage\". \nOn the receiver, I've disabled \"Allow Self\", which seems like it would stop the two receivers/senders from interacting, but it doesn't. \nThis comes up in cases like swords, where you may have multiple receivers and senders sending \"Damage\" to others.\n\nFor an example, see the attached images. I have a big receiver (I know it's big, this is by design) and a small sender (see thing with red circle around it) for \"Damage\". The receiver has allow self disabled, but the big receiver still receives my own \"Damage\" sender.",
